#: ../../electronic/neb.rst:384
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"M1とM3を結ぶ直線上に等間隔に置いたイメージから出発し、FIRE法で各イメージの力の大きさが :math:`10^{-4}` "
"未満になるまで動かした。接線は\\ :eq:`neb-tangent`\\ で求めた。 :numref:`fig-neb-muller-"
"brown`\\ の左図では、CI-NEBのイメージ（丸）が谷底を通って大きく曲がるMEP（実線）に "
"乗っている。射影なしの弾性バンドを硬いばね（:math:`k=2000`、中間イメージ9個）で最小化すると（四角）、 "
"経路はS1を通らずに谷の斜面を横切り、イメージの多くはM1の近くに集まる。"
msgstr ""
"Starting with equally spaced images on the line joining M1 and M3, we "
"used FIRE to move them until the force magnitude on each image fell below"
" :math:`10^{-4}`. We calculated the tangent from Equation \\ :eq:`neb-"
"tangent`\\ . In the left panel of :numref:`fig-neb-muller-brown`\\ , the "
"CI-NEB images (circles) lie on the sharply curved MEP (solid line) along "
"the valley floor. Minimizing the plain elastic band with stiff springs "
"(:math:`k=2000`, nine intermediate images, squares) gives a path that "
"crosses the valley slope without passing through S1, and most images "
"cluster near M1."

#: ../../electronic/neb.rst:390
msgid ""
"左は等高線の上に描いた経路。CI-"
"NEBの点は大きく曲がるMEPに乗り、射影なしの弾性バンドは斜面を直線的に横切る。右はMEPに沿ったエネルギーで、climbing "
"imageが最高点に乗る。"
msgstr ""
"The left panel shows paths overlaid on contours. The CI-NEB points follow"
" the sharply curved MEP, but the plain elastic band cuts straight across "
"the slope. The right panel shows the energy along the MEP, with the "
"climbing image at the highest point."

#: ../../electronic/neb.rst:395
msgid ""
"Müller–Brownポテンシャル上のNEB（M1→M3）。左：等高線（間隔12）と経路。実線はS1から最急降下で 両側へ下って求めたMEP"
"、丸はCI-NEB（中間イメージ9個、:math:`k=50`）、星はclimbing image、 "
"四角は射影なしの弾性バンド（:math:`k=2000`）。右：MEPに沿った弧長とエネルギー。白抜きの丸と菱形は climbing "
"imageを使わないNEB（中間イメージ9個と3個）で、各イメージをMEP上の最も近い点の弧長に置いた。 "
"矢印は順方向と逆方向の障壁、点線は鞍点S1のエネルギー。"
msgstr ""
"NEB on the Müller–Brown potential (M1→M3). The left panel shows the paths"
" over contours at energy intervals of 12. The solid line is the MEP "
"obtained by steepest descent from S1 in both directions. Circles show CI-"
"NEB (nine intermediate images, :math:`k=50`), the star marks the climbing"
" image, and squares show the plain elastic band (:math:`k=2000`). The "
"right panel shows the energy versus arc length along the MEP. Open "
"circles and open diamonds show NEB without a climbing image (nine and "
"three intermediate images, respectively). Each image is plotted at the "
"arc length of the nearest point on the MEP. The arrows show the forward "
"and reverse barriers, and the dotted line marks the energy of saddle "
"point S1."

#: ../../electronic/neb.rst:401
msgid ""
"**イメージの数とclimbing image。** 右図の白抜きの点はMEPの曲線に乗っているが、最高のイメージは "
"鞍点の手前か先にあり、鞍点より低い。climbing imageを加えると、最高のイメージはS1に収束する。"
msgstr ""
"**Number of images and the climbing image.** The open markers in the "
"right panel lie on the MEP curve, but the highest image lies before or "
"after the saddle point and is lower in energy. Adding the climbing image "
"makes the highest image converge to S1."

