#: ../../electronic/neb.rst:421
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"climbing imageを使わないNEBの最高エネルギーは、鞍点より2.0〜2.7低い。この差はイメージを増やしても "
"単調には縮まない。最高のイメージと鞍点の距離は、イメージの並び方が鞍点とどうずれるかで決まるからである。 climbing imageの位置はどの"
" :math:`P` でもS1と :math:`2\\times10^{-7}` 以内で一致した。"
msgstr ""
"The highest energy in NEB without a climbing image is 2.0–2.7 below the "
"saddle-point energy. This difference does not decrease monotonically as "
"images are added, because the distance from the highest image to the "
"saddle point depends on where the saddle falls relative to the sequence "
"of images. For all tested values of :math:`P`, the climbing-image "
"position agreed with S1 to within :math:`2\\times10^{-7}`."

#: ../../electronic/neb.rst:425
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**ばね定数。** 中間イメージ9個のNEBで :math:`k=5,50,500` と変えると、収束した各イメージの位置の差は 最大 "
":math:`1.2\\times10^{-4}` で、隣り合うイメージの間隔はどれも0.1761〜0.1762にそろった。 "
"収束までのステップ数は4532、1218、706と変わった。:eq:`neb-force`\\ から導いた通り、 :math:`k` "
"は収束の速さだけを変える。"
msgstr ""
"**Spring constant.** Varying :math:`k=5,50,500` in NEB with nine "
"intermediate images changed the positions of the converged images by at "
"most :math:`1.2\\times10^{-4}`, and all neighbor spacings fell between "
"0.1761 and 0.1762. The numbers of steps to convergence were 4532, 1218, "
"and 706. As derived from Equation :eq:`neb-force`\\ , :math:`k` changes "
"only the rate of convergence."

#: ../../electronic/neb.rst:430
msgid ""
"**射影なしの弾性バンド。** 同じ9個のイメージで\\ :eq:`neb-elastic-band-objective`\\ を最小化すると、 "
":math:`k=5` では9個すべてがM1かM3から0.1以内へ滑り落ち、最高エネルギーは−80.74で、 "
"M3のエネルギーとほぼ同じになった。バンドは障壁について何も教えない。 :math:`k=2000` "
"ではイメージがMEPから最大0.40離れ、最高エネルギーは−8.95と、 鞍点より31.7高くなった。角切りのために、障壁を大きく見積もる。"
msgstr ""
"**Plain elastic band.** Minimizing the objective in Equation \\ :eq:`neb-"
"elastic-band-objective`\\  with the same nine images and :math:`k=5` made"
" all nine slide to within 0.1 of M1 or M3. The highest energy was −80.74,"
" nearly the energy of M3. The band tells us nothing about the barrier. "
"With :math:`k=2000`, the images were as far as 0.40 from the MEP and the "
"highest energy was −8.95, which is 31.7 above the saddle-point energy. "
"Corner cutting causes an overestimate of the barrier."

#: ../../electronic/neb.rst:436
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**鞍点の確認。** 中間イメージ9個のclimbing imageでヘッセ行列を求めると、固有値は−750.9と490.2で、 "
"負の固有値が1つだけある。その固有ベクトルと\\ :eq:`neb-tangent`\\ の接線の内積の絶対値は0.9985で、 "
"負の曲率の向きは経路に沿っている（この模型の座標は直交座標で、質量の重みは無い）。 この固有ベクトルの向きに両側へ :math:`10^{-3}`"
" だけずらして最急降下で下ると、それぞれM1とM3に着く。 したがってこの点は、M1とM3を結ぶ1次の鞍点である。"
msgstr ""
"**Verifying the saddle point.** The Hessian at the climbing image for "
"nine intermediate images has eigenvalues −750.9 and 490.2, with only one "
"negative eigenvalue. The absolute value of the dot product between the "
"eigenvector for this negative eigenvalue and the tangent from Equation \\"
" :eq:`neb-tangent`\\  is 0.9985, so the direction of negative curvature "
"lies along the path. The model uses Cartesian coordinates with no mass "
"weighting. Displacing by :math:`10^{-3}` along this eigenvector in both "
"directions and following steepest descent leads to M1 and M3, "
"respectively. The point is therefore a first-order saddle point "
"connecting M1 and M3."

#: ../../electronic/neb.rst:442
msgid ""
"**途中の極小。** M1からM2（(0.623, 0.028)、エネルギー−108.17）へ中間イメージ15個でNEBを解くと、 "
"経路はM3から0.020の位置にイメージを置いて通り、その前後に−40.67と−72.48の2つの極大が現れる。 "
"この経路はM1→M3とM3→M2の2回の素過程からなり、M1から経路の最高点までのエネルギー差を、 "
"M1→M2の1回の移動の障壁として扱うことはできない。この例では最初の極大の方が高いので、その差106.03は M1→M3の障壁と一致する。"
msgstr ""
"**Intermediate minimum.** In an NEB calculation from M1 to M2 "
"(coordinates (0.623, 0.028), energy −108.17) with 15 intermediate images,"
" the path passes M3 with an image 0.020 away and has two maxima, one on "
"each side, at −40.67 and −72.48. The path consists of the two elementary "
"steps M1→M3 and M3→M2, so the energy difference between M1 and the "
"highest point along the path cannot be treated as the barrier for a "
"single hop from M1 to M2. In this example the first maximum is higher, so"
" that difference, 106.03, equals the M1→M3 barrier."

#: ../../electronic/neb.rst:451
msgid "解釈と限界"
msgstr "Interpretation and Limitations"

#: ../../electronic/neb.rst:453
msgid ""
"**局所的な探索。** NEBは初期の経路の近くにあるMEPへ収束する。別の鞍点を通る、 "
"障壁のより低い経路が存在しても見つからないことがある。候補の選び方や初期の経路を変えて "
"結果が変わるかで、見落としの有無を判断する。HenkelmanとJónssonのdimer法 [NebDimer1999]_ "
"のように、終状態を指定せずに鞍点を探す方法もある。"
msgstr ""
"**Local search.** NEB converges to an MEP near the initial path. It can "
"miss a lower-barrier path through a different saddle point even if one "
"exists. Change how the candidates are selected or vary the initial path "
"and check whether the result changes to assess whether any paths were "
"missed. Other methods, such as the dimer method of Henkelman and Jónsson "
"[NebDimer1999]_, search for saddle points without specifying the final "
"state."

#: ../../electronic/neb.rst:457
msgid ""
"**0 Kのポテンシャルエネルギー。** NEBの障壁はポテンシャルエネルギー面上の差で、零点振動や "
"振動のエントロピーを含まない。移動の頻度を求めるには、鞍点と極小の振動を使った\\ :ref:`遷移状態理論<transition-state-"
"theory>`\\ が要る。"
msgstr ""
"**Potential energy at 0 K.** An NEB barrier is an energy difference on "
"the potential energy surface and does not include zero-point vibrations "
"or vibrational entropy. Calculating the hop frequency requires \\ "
":ref:`transition state theory <transition-state-theory>`\\  using "
"vibrations at the saddle point and the minimum."

#: ../../electronic/neb.rst:459
msgid ""
"**セルと電荷。** 周期セルで空孔を動かすと、空孔はその周期像とも相互作用する。セルを大きくしたときに "
"障壁が変わるかを調べれば、この相互作用の大きさを見積もれる。イオン結晶で陽イオンを取り除いた 空孔は\\ :ref:`電荷をもちうる"
"<charged-defects>`\\ ので、中性のセルで求めた障壁と荷電した空孔の障壁は一般に異なる。"
msgstr ""
"**Cell and charge.** A vacancy migrating in a periodic cell also "
"interacts with its periodic images. Checking whether the barrier changes "
"with increasing cell size gives an estimate of the size of this "
"interaction. A vacancy created by removing a cation from an ionic crystal"
" \\ :ref:`can carry charge <charged-defects>`\\ , so the barrier from a "
"neutral cell generally differs from that for a charged vacancy."

#: ../../electronic/neb.rst:462
msgid ""
"**エネルギー面の精度。** 鞍点付近の配置は、平衡付近の構造よりエネルギーが高く、原子間の距離も異なる。 "
"機械学習ポテンシャルでは、こうした遷移途中の構造が\\ :ref:`学習データ<mlip-training-data>`\\ に含まれるかで "
"障壁の精度が変わる。`Li₃PO₄のLi空孔移動障壁 <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/li3po4/vacancy-barriers.html>`__\\ が "
"紹介する文献では、移動途中の構造を学習から外すと、DFTとの障壁の差が大きくなった。"
msgstr ""
"**Accuracy of the energy surface.** Configurations near the saddle point "
"are higher in energy than structures near equilibrium and have different "
"interatomic distances. The accuracy of the barrier obtained from a "
"machine learning potential depends on whether such configurations along "
"the transition are included in the \\ :ref:`training data <mlip-training-"
"data>`\\ . The paper discussed in the calculation example `Li Vacancy "
"Migration Barriers in Li₃PO₄ <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/li3po4/vacancy-barriers.html>`__\\  found a larger "
"discrepancy with DFT barriers when configurations along the hop were "
"excluded from training."

#: ../../electronic/neb.rst:466
msgid ""
"**座標の選び方。** :eq:`neb-mep-condition`\\ の「垂直」は座標の内積で決まるので、 "
"直交座標と質量で重み付けした座標とでは、MEPの形が少し変わる。一方、鞍点は力が0の停留点なので、 "
"その位置とエネルギーは座標の選び方によらない。したがって、同じ始点と同じ鞍点を比べる場合、障壁も座標の選び方によらない。"
msgstr ""
"**Choice of coordinates.** In Equation :eq:`neb-mep-condition`\\ , "
"perpendicularity is defined by the coordinate inner product, so the shape"
" of the MEP differs slightly between Cartesian and mass-weighted "
"coordinates. But the saddle point is a stationary point with zero force, "
"so its position and energy do not depend on the choice of coordinates. "
"Thus, the barrier also does not depend on the coordinates when comparing "
"the same starting point and saddle point."

#: ../../electronic/neb.rst:469
msgid ""
"**非晶質の障壁の分布。** 非晶質では経路ごとに障壁が異なり、:eq:`neb-barriers`\\ の値は分布をもつ。 "
"多数回の移動からなる拡散の速さは、障壁の平均ではなく、移動の\\ :ref:`経路がどうつながっているか<thermal-activation-"
"limits>`\\ で決まる。"
msgstr ""
"**Distribution of barriers in amorphous materials.** The barriers vary "
"from path to path in an amorphous material, so the values in Equation :eq"
":`neb-barriers`\\  form a distribution. The rate of diffusion over many "
"hops is determined by the \\ :ref:`connectivity of the migration paths "
"<thermal-activation-limits>`\\ , not by the average barrier."

